{
  "name": "Penta Garden",
  "description": "One-key pentatonic melody machine. Osc1 (Harmo) gives sustained organ warmth; Osc2 (Karplus) adds plucked transients — each note starts with a physical pluck and rings into additive harmonics, like a kalimba in a church. LFO1 Shaper draws a 16-note pentatonic melody over 2 bars (1/8 notes), quantized to minor pentatonic on both oscs. The sequencer runs at 1/8 notes with a C-Eb-F-G-Bb root progression, so the melody transposes through different pentatonic centers — plus 4 automation lanes sculpting filter, reverb, Karplus damping, and unison width across the phrase. Macro 1 (BLOOM) opens everything wide. Macro 2 (DRIFT) slows the melody and smears it into ambient echoes. 108 BPM.",
  "type": "Keys",
  "subtype": "Melodic",
  "author": "Claude",

